sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch10-09> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Complex images lose recognizable features under lossy compression" ;
    dct:description "Under lossy compression by keeping only some basic forms (as in JPEG-like schemes), the relevant features of both simple and completely random images remain recognizable at high compression, whereas images normally considered complex need much lower compression, and reordering the basic forms does not change this substantially." ;
    delphi:context "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 10, “Processes of Perception and Analysis”; section “Irreversible Data Compression” (from p. 572), p. 574. Scope: lossy transform-based image compression of simple, random and complex images" ;
    dct:type "computational-observation" .
}

